  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MOL: Stronger Services, Better chances</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Stronger Services, Better Chances addresses a key gap in Moldova&#x2019;s Child Care Reform: the limited capacity of foster care services to respond to children with complex social and psychological needs. Many foster carers and specialists are not yet equipped to support children with conduct disorders, often linked to Adverse Childhood Experiences. Building on the 2024&#x2013;2025 FCDO-funded initiative, the project will train 70 foster care specialists nationwide and mentor professionals in 8 counties on CARE (Child-Adult Relationship Enhancement) positive parenting programme. In addition, 52 foster carers will receive training&#x2014;either as first-time participants or through refresher sessions&#x2014;and all will benefit from tailored in-person mentoring and follow-up support. Alongside capacity building, the project will advance policy dialogue, drawing on Moldova&#x2019;s endorsement of the Global Charter on Child Care. A multi-stakeholder roundtable will set priorities for extending the 2022&#x2013;2026 National Child Protection Programme beyond 2026. By combining training, mentoring, and advocacy, the project strengthens foster care services and improves outcomes for children.
This project will give foster carers and specialists the tools and confidence to better support children with complex needs, helping them grow in safe and nurturing families. By strengthening services and shaping stronger child protection policies, it creates better chances for children in Moldova to thrive.</narrative>
  </description>
